      "body": "intel-sycl-rt / intel-cmplr-lib-ur install libsycl.so and the UR adapter libs into /opt/venv/lib, but LD_LIBRARY_PATH never pointed there, so torch.xpu.device_count() came back 0 even though Level-Zero saw the GPU fine.\r\n\r\nFixes #48625 \r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Claude\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\ndocker/Dockerfile.xpu builds an image where torch.xpu.device_count() returns 0 even though Level-Zero sees the GPU fine (zeInit/zeDriverGet work). Turns out LD_LIBRARY_PATH (line 139) never includes /opt/venv/lib, which is where the intel-sycl-rt / intel-cmplr-lib-ur pip wheels drop libsycl.so and the UR adapter libs. Without it on the path, SYCL/UR enumeration silently finds 0 devices.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\ndocker build -f docker/Dockerfile.xpu -t vllm-xpu-test .\r\ndocker run --rm --device /dev/dri -it vllm-xpu-test \\\r\n  python -c \"import torch; print(torch.xpu.device_count())\"\r\nthen a normal vllm serve boot on XPU hardware.\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
